    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee8f72b6_eb88f3d0",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T09:23:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is already an exclusion of automation jobs for CI/CD validation, code maintenance, and error detection.\n\nHappy to add more exclusions and exceptions here.",
      "parentUuid": "9c9dfedd_0eb1dcb1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f39b6746_e2bc99b9",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T15:40:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking it would be better to avoid maintaining a list of exclusions here. For example, I think someone mentioned the possibility of automated dependency updates, and while that might be challenging with Google rules today, if Google themselves had such a tool that could automatically update Gerrit whenever their internal deps updated, I think we would welcome that and I don\u0027t think we should have to come update this section.",
      "parentUuid": "ee8f72b6_eb88f3d0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 69
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5bc067a_53a4bc53",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T23:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is too much. Using an agent or script to push a new patch set shouldn\u0027t be prohibited. I\u0027m fine with saying it shouldn\u0027t be fully automated, but if a human reviewed the commits and then says \"push the new patch sets\", I think that should be allowed.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 142,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 143,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f162604c_f56bdead",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T09:23:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done. At the end of the day, we always use _tools_ for pushing code, don\u0027t we? Even running `git push` uses the `git` tool. If you perform a `git push` from your command line or ask the Claude or Gemini tool to do it for you, there isn\u0027t much difference.",
      "parentUuid": "a5bc067a_53a4bc53",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 142,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 143,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f6ea3cb_265995fe",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002666
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T23:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, I pretty strongly disagree with this one. I get the desire to prevent slop, but this isn\u0027t the right way to do it. I see nothing wrong with any contributor using AI to generate a commit message, so long as they understand it and can answer reasonable questions about it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d1074be4_b7520c51",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T09:23:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "@matthias.sohn@gmail.com what is your view?",
      "parentUuid": "3f6ea3cb_265995fe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "17f146a5_3e749da1",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003873
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T11:36:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with Nasser here: there is nothing bad if the AI proposes a commit message. Of course, I check the result. The resulting commit message is often grammatically significantly better than the one I would write as a non-native english speaker.",
      "parentUuid": "d1074be4_b7520c51",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6e179623_3b0cf36d",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T13:34:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are we in agreement if we reformulate it as: _\"The commit message can be written by the human contributor with the assistance of AI, as long as the human is in control of the meaning and the intended objective\"_?\n\nBasically, we are OK with the human + AI cooperating to write the commit message, with the human staying in the driver\u0027s seat.\n\n@matthias.sohn@gmail.com @nasser.grainawi@oss.qualcomm.com?",
      "parentUuid": "17f146a5_3e749da1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c58cc11_a099bffc",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003873
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T14:39:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or maybe something like: the commit message is considered part of the change and, just like the source code, must be fully understood by the contributor.\n\nI mean, there is probably no need to distinguish commit message part from the source code part.",
      "parentUuid": "6e179623_3b0cf36d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3380ed9a_c50a1889",
        "filename": "Documentation/dev-contributing.txt",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 146,
      "author": {
        "id": 1006192
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T14:45:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Or maybe something like: the commit message is considered part of the change and, just like the source code, must be fully understood by the contributor.\n\u003e \n\u003e I mean, there is probably no need to distinguish commit message part from the source code part.\n\nI believe the commit message is more similar to the _prompt_ you give to AI: it should describe what you would like to achieve rather than the implementation.\n\nWhilst I am OK with people contributing 100% AI-generated code without supervision, as long as the contributor can say that it corresponds to what they want and agree with the quality of the implementation, I am not comfortable when the commit message is driven by the AI model and is fully 100% AI-generated without supervision.\n\nThe code *does something*, but the commit message is way more important, IMHO, because it shows what the author of the change wants to achieve and what the change is expected to deliver.\n\nI am fine with using AI to improve and control the form of the commit message, but I am not comfortable with AI driving everything, including the intended objective of the change (the commit message).",
      "parentUuid": "7c58cc11_a099bffc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 146,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "1ade253d3c4f72a64679b24c7c54c89280d54b3d",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
